1
00:00:00,680 --> 00:00:09,280
Long ago there was a kind, diligent young woodcutter.

2
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:17,310
Every day he went to forest to chop wood to earn living.

3
00:00:17,310 --> 00:00:25,110
One day, he swung axe to chop a dry tree, axe blade flew into river.

4
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:37,080
River deep, water fast, hard to dive in.

5
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:44,370
Suddenly, an old gray-haired old man appeared. Hearing woodcutter's story, old man said

6
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:49,060
Suddenly, an old gray-haired old man appeared. Hearing woodcutter's story, old man said: - I can retrieve axe for you.

7
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:52,420
As soon as he finished, old man jumped into river.

8
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:56,800
In a blink, he raised a shining golden axe blade.

9
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,480
Is this your axe? - Old man asked.

10
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:08,530
Grandpa, this axe blade is not mine.

11
00:01:08,530 --> 00:01:14,480
Old man again dove into river and raised a shining silver axe blade.

12
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:16,750
Surely this is your axe?

13
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:23,930
Grandpa, this axe blade is also not mine.

14
00:01:23,930 --> 00:01:28,460
Old man dove again and raised an iron axe blade.

15
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:30,970
Woodcutter just saw it quickly shouted

16
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:38,240
- This is my axe blade. I thank you grandpa.

17
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:41,530
You are an honest, truthful person.

18
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:50,680
I give you these golden and silver axe blades.

19
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:56,350
Woodcutter hadn't finished thanking when old man disappeared.

20
00:01:56,350 --> 00:02:04,530
Then he knew he had been helped by Buddha.

